From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:30:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_hqdn3d_vulkan: add a Vulkan hqdn3d filter

Add hqdn3d_vulkan, the hqdn3d denoiser in two compute shaders: a
horizontal pass for the spatial line filter and a vertical pass for the
spatial column filter and the temporal filter. It runs the same integer
lookup tables as the CPU filter, which now come from hqdn3d_coefs.c so
that both filters share one implementation, and it takes the same
options and commands.

The output is bit-exact to hqdn3d for the planar 8, 10, 12 and 16 bit
formats, and for nv12, p010, p012 and p016 against hqdn3d on the
equivalent planar format. As in hqdn3d, a planar output sample is
narrowed to the width of its 8 or 16 bit container, so a temporal
result below zero is stored as hqdn3d stores it. The one exception:
where the CPU filter writes a value above the format maximum into a 10
or 12 bit plane, p010 and p012 cannot store it, and this filter writes
the format maximum instead.

The temporal state is dropped where hqdn3d drops it: on graph
configuration and on a change of frame size within the stream. After a
size change, and for a first frame whose size differs from the link,
the output frames come from a frames context of the frame size. A
frame whose format differs from the link's, the first frame included,
is refused with AVERROR(EINVAL), as hqdn3d refuses a change of format
within the stream.

At initialization the filter refuses with AVERROR(ENOTSUP) a device
created without a shader or storage feature the shaders use, and a
frame size whose sample buffers exceed the device's
maxStorageBufferRange. A failed initialization, or a failed
reallocation after a size change, is final.

This is the content of FFmpeg pull request 25879, adapted to the 9.0
release: the fail path discards the execution context with
ff_vk_exec_discard_deps(), the host wait after each submission orders
the temporal history between frames (this release has no timeline
semaphore on FFVkExecContext), the filter does not declare
FF_FILTER_FLAG_DYNAMIC_FRAME_SIZE, which this release does not have,
and the Changelog is left alone.

libavfilter/tests/hqdn3d_vulkan runs hqdn3d and hqdn3d_vulkan side by
side on frames of three sizes and compares every output frame; it also
checks the first-frame size change, the format refusal, the p012 clamp
and a temporal result below zero. It runs under fate-hw as
fate-filter-hqdn3d-vulkan when hqdn3d_vulkan and hqdn3d are enabled.

The filter ports GPL code and therefore depends on --enable-gpl, as
hqdn3d does.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
